Package: geevis
Title: Google Earth Engine, Satellite and Drone Imagery, and Vegetation Indices
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Wagner", "Faria Barbosa", , "barbosawf@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8725-2099"))
Description: Tools to go from imagery to plot-level tables of bands and
    vegetation indices. Sets up the Python environment and authentication
    that 'rgee' needs for Google Earth Engine, downloads and summarises
    satellite bands and vegetation indices over polygon regions and
    phenological phases, extracts the same from local (e.g. drone) rasters
    with optional vegetation segmentation by Otsu, triangle or k-means
    thresholds, merges overlapping rasters, and ships a built-in table of
    vegetation index equations. Includes a trilingual (Portuguese,
    English, Spanish) cheat sheet, gee_tips().
